  <!-- Get started -->
  <section class="o2-install" id="get-started">
    <p class="kick">08 — Get started</p>
    <h2 class="h2">Up and running in one command</h2>
    <p class="o2-install-lede">
      All you need is a box that runs Docker — a Linux server, a NAS, or the
      Mac&nbsp;mini in the corner. Let the installer do the work, or write the
      compose file yourself.
    </p>

    <div class="o2-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Installation method">
      <button class="o2-tab is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-panel="oneliner">One-liner</button>
      <button class="o2-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-panel="compose">Docker Compose</button>
    </div>

    <div class="o2-panel is-active" id="panel-oneliner" role="tabpanel">
      <figure class="macwin o2-term">
        <div class="bar">
          <div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <button class="o2-copy" data-copy="code-oneliner" aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="viewport">
          <pre class="o2-code" id="code-oneliner">curl -fsSL https://cloud.orbit.cosmique.io/install.sh | bash</pre>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <ul class="o2-install-points">
        <li>Checks for Docker, writes a compose stack to <code>/opt/orbit</code>, pulls the image and starts the server.</li>
        <li>Give it a domain and it provisions HTTPS automatically. Skip it and you get plain HTTP on port&nbsp;9899.</li>
        <li>No magic left behind — the result is a plain <code>docker-compose.yml</code> you own from day one.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="o2-panel" id="panel-compose" role="tabpanel">
      <figure class="macwin o2-term">
        <div class="bar">
          <div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <button class="o2-copy" data-copy="code-compose" aria-label="Copy compose file">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="viewport">
          <pre class="o2-code" id="code-compose">services:
  orbit:
    image: ghcr.io/cosmique-source/orbit:edge
    container_name: orbit
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "9899:9899"
    environment:
      - TZ=UTC
    volumes:
      - /path/to/your/music:/music:ro   <span class="c"># your library</span>
      - orbit_data:/data                <span class="c"># database &amp; server keys</span>
volumes:
  orbit_data:</pre>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <ul class="o2-install-points">
        <li>Save as <code>docker-compose.yml</code>, point the volume at your collection, then <code>docker compose up&nbsp;-d</code>.</li>
        <li>Orbit is at <code>http://localhost:9899</code> — open it, scan your library, pair your apps.</li>
        <li>Drop the <code>:ro</code> if you want Orbit to organize files during import.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

